## CURRENT STATE

- `frontend/` + `backend/` remain the served product. The public Netlify
  `frontend-next/` beta is separate and is not the Phase 13 cutover.
- Migration numbering is authoritative: Phase 11 = admitted AI extensions,
  Phase 12 = Club/Community, Phase 13 = Cutover.
- PR #65 was squash-merged into `main` as
  `786f437fc54b8d44c9003a43d7f4bbd097d8455e` after all relevant CI checks
  passed. Personal profile photos are live in `frontend-next/` as an
  explicitly admitted named exception; the six curated preset avatars remain
  available.
- Prepared photos are decoded in the browser, center-cropped, resized to
  512 x 512 and freshly encoded as WebP at quality 0.86. Input is limited to
  JPEG, PNG or WebP and 5 MB; re-encoding decoded pixels removes original
  EXIF and other source metadata.
- Stored custom-avatar references use the canonical form
  `<profile-uuid>/<object-uuid>.webp`; the database never stores a full
  project URL. Persistence and rendering accept a custom reference only when
  its owner folder matches the declaring profile; arbitrary, external,
  foreign-owner and malformed values fail closed to initials.
- Save ordering is upload new object, update profile, then delete the obsolete
  custom object. Failed profile updates compensate by deleting the new object;
  failed post-update cleanup preserves the new profile state and surfaces a
  warning.
- Migration `20260821183000_profile_avatars.sql` was applied by the Supabase
  GitHub integration at merge and is the latest row in the production ledger
  of project `pijnmcllmfgjmgsvtcej`.
- Effective production objects were reread after deployment: bucket
  `avatar-profili` is public with a 5242880-byte limit and `image/webp` as the
  only allowed MIME type; the four `avatar_profili_*` policies grant public
  read to anon and authenticated and confine insert/update/delete to the
  caller's own folder; `profiles_avatar_url_vinea_check` exists and is
  validated; `profiles` RLS is unchanged (`profiles_select_own`,
  `profiles_update_own`) and the authenticated UPDATE grant still covers
  exactly the same eight columns.
- The pre-merge preflight found 10 empty `avatar_url` values and 1
  `/avatar/calice.svg`, zero values incompatible with the CHECK, and no
  pre-existing bucket or avatar policies. No existing data was rewritten.
- Final local verification with Bun 1.3.14 passed: lint with 14 warnings (13
  pre-existing plus the deliberate `<img>` for blob/Storage avatar URLs) and
  no errors, typecheck, 556 tests with zero failures, build and
  `git diff --check`. The `frontend-next` CI floor and its regression
  contract are aligned at 556.
- The authenticated browser smoke test was NOT run: no usable session for the
  existing test account was available in this environment, and no new account
  or fixture was created.
- Deliberate historical verification residues remain: one test bottle in state
  `aperta`, the test account, and three objects in each of its `cantina` and
  `annunci` folders.

